<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Australia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Australia is a continent and country in the southern hemisphere. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> began colonising it in 1788 with a penal settlement at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sydney-nova-scotia">Sydney</a>, and several self-governing colonies developed in the nineteenth century, uniting as the Commonwealth of Australia in 1901. It became one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>'s major <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominion">dominions</a> and settler societies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/australia.jpg" alt="Australia" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown (Vector graphics image by Ian Fieggen) (only minor code changes by uploader.) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Australia_(converted).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
